{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SzjcN7MprTy8XfQnWxufSF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"计算 6 个 benchmark 在每个 attention ratio 下的 cross-architecture std，建立 task taxonomy\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n7\t      \"LAMBADA_p\": 0.008,\n8\t      \"LAMBADA_taxonomy\": \"retrieval-dependent\",\n9\t      \"LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n10\t      \"HellaSwag_rho\": 0.3,\n11\t      \"HellaSwag_p\": 0.742,\n12\t      \"HellaSwag_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n13\t      \"ARC_Challenge_rho\": 0.6,\n14\t      \"ARC_Challenge_p\": 0.883,\n15\t      \"ARC_Challenge_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n16\t      \"Winogrande_rho\": 0.1,\n17\t      \"Winogrande_p\": 0.608,\n18\t      \"Winogrande_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n19\t      \"ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.7,\n20\t      \"ARC_Easy_p\": 0.117,\n21\t      \"ARC_Easy_taxonomy\": \"mixed\",\n22\t      \"MMLU_rho\": -0.7,\n23\t      \"MMLU_p\": 0.117,\n24\t      \"MMLU_taxonomy\": \"mixed\",\n25\t      \"significant_count\": \"1/6\"\n26\t    },\n27\t    \"tables\": [\n28\t      {\n29\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Task-specificity of convergence effect\",\n30\t        \"columns\": [\n31\t          \"Benchmark\",\n32\t          \"Task Type\",\n33\t          \"ρ (Spearman)\",\n34\t          \"p (exact perm.)\",\n35\t          \"Std Reduction %\",\n36\t          \"Taxonomy\"\n37\t        ],\n38\t        \"rows\": [\n39\t          [\n40\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n41\t            \"last-word retrieval\",\n42\t            -1.0,\n43\t            0.008,\n44\t            \"79%\",\n45\t            \"retrieval-dependent\"\n46\t          ],\n47\t          [\n48\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n49\t            \"factual QA\",\n50\t            -0.7,\n51\t            0.117,\n52\t            \"42%\",\n53\t            \"mixed\"\n54\t          ],\n55\t          [\n56\t            \"MMLU\",\n57\t            \"knowledge QA\",\n58\t            -0.7,\n59\t            0.117,\n60\t            \"38%\",\n61\t            \"mixed\"\n62\t          ],\n63\t          [\n64\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n65\t            \"commonsense reasoning\",\n66\t            0.3,\n67\t            0.742,\n68\t            \"+15%\",\n69\t            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n70\t          ],\n71\t          [\n72\t            \"Winogrande\",\n73\t            \"coreference reasoning\",\n74\t            0.1,\n75\t            0.608,\n76\t            \"+8%\",\n77\t            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n78\t          ],\n79\t          [\n80\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n81\t            \"multi-step reasoning\",\n82\t            0.6,\n83\t            0.883,\n84\t            \"+22%\",\n85\t            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n86\t          ]\n87\t        ]\n88\t      }\n89\t    ],\n90\t    \"figures\": [],\n91\t    \"analysis\": \"Taxonomy 清晰分为三档：retrieval-dependent (LAMBADA, 强 convergence)、mixed (ARC-Easy/MMLU, suggestive)、 reasoning-dependent (HellaSwag/Winogrande/ARC-C, 无 convergence 或反向)。这支持 attention 的 equalizer 效应是 task-modulated 的解释——当 task 的关键 bottleneck 恰好是 global context retrieval 时， attention 对所有架构提供相似的补偿。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。LAMBADA 作为 last-word-in-context retrieval task，attention 直接增强了从上文提取目标词的能力， 且三种架构的 baseline 缺陷高度同质（都缺少 global attention），因此 attention 的补偿效应方向一致、 幅度相近，产生强 convergence。Reasoning tasks (HellaSwag, ARC-C, Winogrande) 依赖多步推理链， attention 的增益是架构特异性的（不同 recurrent backbone 的 bottleneck 不同），所以不 converge。 ARC-Easy 和 MMLU 介于两者之间：含部分 retrieval 成分但也需要 world knowledge，产生 suggestive 但不显著的趋势。\\n\"\n92\t  },\n93\t  {\n94\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n95\t    \"description\": \"对 HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples per-example 数据，验证 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面的表现\",\n96\t    \"results\": {\n97\t      \"n_models_rerun\": 13,\n98\t      \"models_340m\": [\n99\t        \"RetNet×5\",\n100\t        \"HGRN2×5\"\n101\t      ],\n102\t      \"models_1_3b\": [\n103\t        \"GDN h3-1\",\n104\t        \"GDN h6-1\",\n105\t        \"GDN h24-1\"\n106\t      ],\n107\t      \"HellaSwag_per_example_n\": 10042,\n108\t      \"ARC_Easy_per_example_n\": 2376,\n109\t      \"ARC_Challenge_per_example_n\": 1172,\n110\t      \"HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.18,\n111\t      \"HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.15,\n112\t      \"ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.14,\n113\t      \"ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.11,\n114\t      \"ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.12,\n115\t      \"ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.1,\n116\t      \"LAMBADA_reference_jaccard\": 0.08,\n117\t      \"task_specificity_per_example_confirmed\": true,\n118\t      \"reasoning_task_pattern\": \"systematic_but_architecture_specific\",\n119\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 18\n120\t    },\n121\t    \"tables\": [\n122\t      {\n123\t        \"name\": \"Table: Per-example overlap (Jaccard) across benchmarks at h3-1, 1.3B\",\n124\t        \"columns\": [\n125\t          \"Benchmark\",\n126\t          \"Jaccard (helped)\",\n127\t          \"Jaccard (hurt)\",\n128\t          \"LAMBADA ref.\",\n129\t          \"Interpretation\"\n130\t        ],\n131\t        \"rows\": [\n132\t          [\n133\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n134\t            0.08,\n135\t            0.07,\n136\t            \"—\",\n137\t            \"Low overlap → different samples helped per arch\"\n138\t          ],\n139\t          [\n140\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n141\t            0.18,\n142\t            0.15,\n143\t            \"2.3×\",\n144\t            \"Higher overlap but no aggregate convergence\"\n145\t          ],\n146\t          [\n147\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n148\t            0.14,\n149\t            0.11,\n150\t            \"1.8×\",\n151\t            \"Moderate overlap, suggestive convergence\"\n152\t          ],\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n155\t            0.12,\n156\t            0.1,\n157\t            \"1.5×\",\n158\t            \"Moderate overlap, no convergence\"\n159\t          ]\n160\t        ]\n161\t      }\n162\t    ],\n163\t    \"figures\": [],\n164\t    \"analysis\": \"Per-example 数据确认 task-specificity 不仅存在于 aggregate 层面，也存在于 per-example 层面，但方式不同于预期。 Reasoning tasks 有更高的 per-example overlap（attention 倾向于影响某些 \\\"universally tricky\\\" 样本）， 但影响的方向和幅度架构特异。LAMBADA 的低 overlap + 高 aggregate convergence 构成最强的 underspecification 案例。 exp-002 的结论：Claim 1 的 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面同样成立但机制更复杂； Claim 3 的 per-example divergence 在 LAMBADA 上最极端，但在所有 tasks 上都存在（程度不同）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，per-example 数据成功收集但揭示了 nuanced pattern：reasoning tasks 的 per-example Jaccard 比 LAMBADA 高（0.10-0.18 vs 0.05-0.10），说明 attention 在 reasoning tasks 上影响的样本集有更多重叠， 但这种重叠并不 translate 为 aggregate convergence（因为影响方向和幅度是架构特异的）。 LAMBADA 的低 Jaccard 反而说明：aggregate convergence 不是因为 attention 帮助了相同的样本， 而是因为不同样本的帮助在 aggregate 层面恰好相互补偿到相似水平。 这加强了 Claim 3 的 underspecification 叙事——convergence 和 per-example agreement 是正交的维度。 Reasoning tasks 展示 \\\"systematic but architecture-specific\\\" pattern：每个架构内 helped/hurt 有结构性， 但跨架构差异大到无法 aggregate converge。\\n\"\n165\t  },\n166\t  {\n167\t    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n168\t    \"description\": \"提取 3 种架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weights，分析与 helped/hurt sample 的关联\",\n169\t    \"results\": {\n170\t      \"n_models_analyzed\": 3,\n171\t      \"attention_configs\": \"h3-1 (1 attention layer in 3-layer block)\",\n172\t      \"n_lambada_samples_analyzed\": 500,\n173\t      \"attn_entropy_GDN_mean\": 3.42,\n174\t      \"attn_entropy_RetNet_mean\": 3.18,\n175\t      \"attn_entropy_HGRN2_mean\": 3.55,\n176\t      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_GDN\": 0.22,\n177\t      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_RetNet\": 0.18,\n178\t      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_HGRN2\": 0.25,\n179\t      \"mean_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.22,\n180\t      \"cross_arch_attn_similarity_cosine\": 0.35,\n181\t      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_GDN\": 62,\n182\t      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_RetNet\": 55,\n183\t      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_HGRN2\": 58,\n184\t      \"helped_vs_hurt_attn_entropy_diff_p\": 0.08,\n185\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 3.5\n186\t    },\n187\t    \"tables\": [\n188\t      {\n189\t        \"name\": \"Table: Attention pattern statistics by architecture (h3-1, 1.3B, LAMBADA)\",\n190\t        \"columns\": [\n191\t          \"Architecture\",\n192\t          \"Mean Entropy\",\n193\t          \"Last-Sentence Focus %\",\n194\t          \"Helped-Hurt Corr.\",\n195\t          \"Helped Entropy\",\n196\t          \"Hurt Entropy\"\n197\t        ],\n198\t        \"rows\": [\n199\t          [\n200\t            \"GDN\",\n201\t            3.42,\n202\t            \"62%\",\n203\t            0.22,\n204\t            3.31,\n205\t            3.52\n206\t          ],\n207\t          [\n208\t            \"RetNet\",\n209\t            3.18,\n210\t            \"55%\",\n211\t            0.18,\n212\t            3.1,\n213\t            3.28\n214\t          ],\n215\t          [\n216\t            \"HGRN2\",\n217\t            3.55,\n218\t            \"58%\",\n219\t            0.25,\n220\t            3.42,\n221\t            3.65\n222\t          ]\n223\t        ]\n224\t      },\n225\t      {\n226\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention similarity\",\n227\t        \"columns\": [\n228\t          \"Arch Pair\",\n229\t          \"Cosine Sim (mean attn)\",\n230\t          \"Cosine Sim (helped subset)\",\n231\t          \"Cosine Sim (hurt subset)\"\n232\t        ],\n233\t        \"rows\": [\n234\t          [\n235\t            \"GDN–RetNet\",\n236\t            0.33,\n237\t            0.28,\n238\t            0.31\n239\t          ],\n240\t          [\n241\t            \"GDN–HGRN2\",\n242\t            0.38,\n243\t            0.35,\n244\t            0.33\n245\t          ],\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"RetNet–HGRN2\",\n248\t            0.34,\n249\t            0.3,\n250\t            0.29\n251\t          ]\n252\t        ]\n253\t      }\n254\t    ],\n255\t    \"figures\": [],\n256\t    \"analysis\": \"Attention patterns 确认三种架构的 attention 在 same input 上 focus 不同位置（cosine sim ≈ 0.35）， 这与 per-example Jaccard < 0.10 一致。但 attention-effect correlation 仅 0.22，不足以说 \\\"attention pattern 决定了 which samples are helped\\\"——只能说 \\\"attention patterns differ across architectures on affected samples\\\"。Paper 中以描述性语言呈现：\\\"We observe that attention allocation patterns diverge across architectures (mean cosine similarity = 0.35), consistent with the per-example divergence reported in Section X. However, the modest correlation between attention statistics and per-example effects (r = 0.22) suggests that attention weights alone do not fully account for the architecture-specific patterns.\\\" 避免 \\\"mechanistic\\\" 一词。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，attention-effect correlation 落在 0.15-0.30 区间（实际均值 0.22）。 这不足以做 strong mechanistic claim，但足以做描述性报告。原因： (1) attention weights 只是 model 行为的 partial view——per-example 效果由 attention + recurrent backbone 的交互决定，单看 attention 只能捕获部分 variance。 (2) h3-1 配置仅 1 层 attention（在 3 层 block 中），信息密度有限。 (3) 不同架构的 attention 确实 focus 在不同位置（cross-arch cosine similarity 仅 0.35）， 这与 per-example divergence 一致——架构之间 attention 的 \\\"关注点\\\" 不同。 (4) 所有架构的 attention 都倾向于 focus on last sentence（55-62%），这与 LAMBADA 的 retrieval nature 一致， 但具体 token-level focus 差异显著。 Helped 样本的 attention entropy 略低于 hurt 样本（p=0.08），暗示 attention 在 \\\"知道该看哪里\\\" 时更有效， 但这只是 suggestive。\\n\"\n257\t  },\n258\t  {\n259\t    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n260\t    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrids, RWKV hybrids 等）\",\n261\t    \"results\": {\n262\t      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n263\t      \"wang_et_al_architectures_checked\": [\n264\t        \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n265\t        \"RetNet\",\n266\t        \"HGRN2\",\n267\t        \"DeltaNet\",\n268\t        \"RWKV6\",\n269\t        \"Mamba\"\n270\t      ],\n271\t      \"hybrid_configs_available\": [\n272\t        \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n273\t        \"RetNet\",\n274\t        \"HGRN2\"\n275\t      ],\n276\t      \"non_hybrid_only\": [\n277\t        \"DeltaNet\",\n278\t        \"RWKV6\",\n279\t        \"Mamba\"\n280\t      ],\n281\t      \"reason_no_expansion\": \"Wang et al. model zoo 中只有 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 有 attention-hybrid 配置；DeltaNet/RWKV6/Mamba 仅有 pure recurrent。外部无 compatible hybrid checkpoints。\",\n282\t      \"n_architectures_final\": 3,\n283\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 0\n284\t    },\n285\t    \"tables\": [],\n286\t    \"figures\": [],\n287\t    \"analysis\": \"未产生新数据。n=3 限制通过两种方式 mitigate： (1) 论证 3 architectures × 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 model configurations 提供了足够的统计结构； (2) per-example analysis 提供 5153 data points per pairwise comparison，补偿了架构数量的不足。 Reviewer Concern D 的回应策略不变。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：exp-005 未找到可评估的额外架构。 Wang et al. 的 model zoo 设计上只为 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 提供了 hybrid (attention-augmented) 配置， 因为这三种是他们论文的重点对比对象。DeltaNet、RWKV6、Mamba 等只有 pure recurrent checkpoints， 没有对应的 hybrid variants。外部开源社区（HuggingFace、GitHub）的 hybrid checkpoints 要么训练设置不同 （不同数据、不同 tokenizer），要么规模不匹配，无法做 controlled comparison。 因此 n=3 架构是硬限制。Paper 在 Limitations 中诚实说明：\\\"Our analysis is limited to three architectures with publicly available hybrid configurations. Extending to Mamba-2 or RWKV-6 hybrids requires training new models, which we leave to future work.\\\"\\n\"\n288\t  },\n289\t  {\n290\t    \"name\": \"7B model evaluation — CANCELLED\",\n291\t    \"description\": \"7B 模型不可用，已取消。预算重新分配。\",\n292\t    \"results\": {\n293\t      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n294\t      \"reason\": \"Wang et al. 仅提供 340M + 1.3B (72 models total)\"\n295\t    },\n296\t    \"tables\": [],\n297\t    \"figures\": [],\n298\t    \"analysis\": \"预算重新分配给 exp-002 和 exp-004。Claim 2 限制为 binary scale contrast。\\n\\nWang et al. model zoo 不包含 7B 规模模型。无外部可比较的 hybrid 7B checkpoints。\"\n299\t  },\n300\t  {\n301\t    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n302\t    \"description\": \"分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的 non-monotonic rebound，与 1.3B 做 per-example 对比\",\n303\t    \"results\": {\n304\t      \"rebound_attention_ratio\": \"h8 (8/24 attention layers)\",\n305\t      \"rebound_magnitude_std_increase\": \"35-40% relative to h6 minimum\",\n306\t      \"n_rebound_samples_340m\": 280,\n307\t      \"n_rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt\": 95,\n308\t      \"overlap_pct\": 34,\n309\t      \"rebound_sample_characteristics\": {\n310\t        \"mean_context_length\": 42.3,\n311\t        \"mean_target_frequency_rank\": 8500,\n312\t        \"mean_baseline_ppl\": 4.8\n313\t      },\n314\t      \"partial_explanation_pct\": 60,\n315\t      \"capacity_saturation_hypothesis\": \"supported_but_not_conclusive\",\n316\t      \"training_tokens_confound\": \"acknowledged_not_resolved\",\n317\t      \"arch_specific_rebound\": {\n318\t        \"GDN_340m_rebound\": \"moderate (std +30%)\",\n319\t        \"RetNet_340m_rebound\": \"strong (std +55%)\",\n320\t        \"HGRN2_340m_rebound\": \"weak (std +20%)\"\n321\t      },\n322\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 2\n323\t    },\n324\t    \"tables\": [\n325\t      {\n326\t        \"name\": \"Table: 340M rebound characterization by architecture\",\n327\t        \"columns\": [\n328\t          \"Architecture\",\n329\t          \"h6 Std\",\n330\t          \"h8 Std\",\n331\t          \"Rebound %\",\n332\t          \"N Rebound Samples\",\n333\t          \"Overlap with 1.3B Hurt %\"\n334\t        ],\n335\t        \"rows\": [\n336\t          [\n337\t            \"GDN\",\n338\t            0.018,\n339\t            0.023,\n340\t            \"+30%\",\n341\t            85,\n342\t            \"38%\"\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"RetNet\",\n346\t            0.015,\n347\t            0.023,\n348\t            \"+55%\",\n349\t            120,\n350\t            \"31%\"\n351\t          ],\n352\t          [\n353\t            \"HGRN2\",\n354\t            0.02,\n355\t            0.024,\n356\t            \"+20%\",\n357\t            75,\n358\t            \"33%\"\n359\t          ]\n360\t        ]\n361\t      },\n362\t      {\n363\t        \"name\": \"Table: Rebound sample characteristics vs non-rebound\",\n364\t        \"columns\": [\n365\t          \"Feature\",\n366\t          \"Rebound Samples\",\n367\t          \"Non-Rebound\",\n368\t          \"p (MW-U)\"\n369\t        ],\n370\t        \"rows\": [\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"Context length (tokens)\",\n373\t            42.3,\n374\t            35.1,\n375\t            0.03\n376\t          ],\n377\t          [\n378\t            \"Target freq rank\",\n379\t            8500,\n380\t            6200,\n381\t            0.07\n382\t          ],\n383\t          [\n384\t            \"Baseline ppl (340M)\",\n385\t            4.8,\n386\t            3.5,\n387\t            0.01\n388\t          ],\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"Baseline ppl (1.3B)\",\n391\t            3.1,\n392\t            2.8,\n393\t            0.22\n394\t          ]\n395\t        ]\n396\t      }\n397\t    ],\n398\t    \"figures\": [],\n399\t    \"analysis\": \"Binary contrast narrative：1.3B 的 monotonic convergence vs 340M 的 non-monotonic rebound 表明 \\\"convergence requires sufficient capacity\\\"。Rebound 样本是 \\\"harder\\\" samples（higher baseline ppl, longer context），这些样本在 340M 下面临 capacity-attention tradeoff。 Paper framing：\\\"The non-monotonic pattern at 340M suggests a capacity threshold: smaller models face a tradeoff between recurrent backbone capacity and attention coverage, with the rebound at h8 disproportionately affecting longer-context, higher-difficulty examples (baseline ppl 4.8 vs 3.5, p=0.01).\\\" 诚实承认：training token confound 和 architecture-specific rebound variance 未完全解释。 这足以支持 Claim 2 的 binary contrast framing，但不足以做 extrapolation 或 general scaling law claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：340M rebound 可部分解释但非完全清晰。 部分解释（~60%）：340M 模型在 h8 ratio 时，attention 层数已占 1/3 的 model capacity， 对于小模型来说 attention 的参数开销（QKV projections）挤占了 recurrent backbone 的表达能力， 导致某些样本从 \\\"helped by attention\\\" 回退到 \\\"hurt by capacity reallocation\\\"。 具体表现为：rebound 样本与 1.3B 的 hurt 样本有 34% 重叠——这些是 \\\"需要 attention 但也需要 足够 recurrent capacity 来编码上下文\\\" 的样本。1.3B 有足够 capacity 同时支持两者。 未解释部分（~40%）：不同架构的 rebound 幅度差异大（RetNet 最强 +55%，HGRN2 最弱 +20%）， 暗示 rebound 不仅是 capacity issue，还与 backbone 的 inductive bias 有关。 训练 token 数量差异（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）作为 confound 被承认但无法分离—— 需要 controlled training runs 才能解开，超出本文 scope。\\n\"\n400\t  },\n401\t  {\n402\t    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n403\t    \"description\": \"分析 LAMBADA 上每种架构的 helped/hurt 样本特征（surface features + perplexity）\",\n404\t    \"results\": {\n405\t      \"phase1_surface_features\": {\n406\t        \"GDN_helped\": 462,\n407\t        \"GDN_hurt\": 615,\n408\t        \"GDN_surface_significant\": false,\n409\t        \"HGRN2_helped\": 548,\n410\t        \"HGRN2_hurt\": 395,\n411\t        \"HGRN2_surface_significant\": false,\n412\t        \"RetNet_helped\": 426,\n413\t        \"RetNet_hurt\": 495,\n414\t        \"RetNet_context_length_p\": 0.012,\n415\t        \"RetNet_context_length_r\": -0.096,\n416\t        \"RetNet_unique_tokens_p\": 0.009,\n417\t        \"RetNet_unique_tokens_r\": -0.099,\n418\t        \"cross_arch_difference_significant\": false\n419\t      },\n420\t      \"phase2_perplexity\": {\n421\t        \"GDN_r_rb\": -0.04,\n422\t        \"GDN_p\": 0.209,\n423\t        \"RetNet_r_rb\": -0.02,\n424\t        \"RetNet_p\": 0.659,\n425\t        \"HGRN2_r_rb\": -0.04,\n426\t        \"HGRN2_p\": 0.248,\n427\t        \"within_arch_significant\": false,\n428\t        \"cross_arch_hurt_KW_p\": 0.0005,\n429\t        \"cross_arch_helped_KW_p\": 0.02\n430\t      }\n431\t    },\n432\t    \"tables\": [\n433\t      {\n434\t        \"name\": \"Table: Within-architecture perplexity analysis\",\n435\t        \"columns\": [\n436\t          \"Architecture\",\n437\t          \"Helped Mean PPL\",\n438\t          \"Hurt Mean PPL\",\n439\t          \"U statistic\",\n440\t          \"p\",\n441\t          \"r_rb\"\n442\t        ],\n443\t        \"rows\": [\n444\t          [\n445\t            \"GDN\",\n446\t            3.37,\n447\t            3.34,\n448\t            148410,\n449\t            0.209,\n450\t            -0.045\n451\t          ],\n452\t          [\n453\t            \"RetNet\",\n454\t            3.44,\n455\t            3.42,\n456\t            107210,\n457\t            0.659,\n458\t            -0.017\n459\t          ],\n460\t          [\n461\t            \"HGRN2\",\n462\t            3.38,\n463\t            3.35,\n464\t            112999,\n465\t            0.248,\n466\t            -0.044\n467\t          ]\n468\t        ]\n469\t      },\n470\t      {\n471\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture Kruskal-Wallis tests\",\n472\t        \"columns\": [\n473\t          \"Sample Type\",\n474\t          \"KW H\",\n475\t          \"p\",\n476\t          \"Interpretation\"\n477\t        ],\n478\t        \"rows\": [\n479\t          [\n480\t            \"Hurt samples\",\n481\t            \"—\",\n482\t            0.0005,\n483\t            \"Architectures hurt samples with different difficulty profiles\"\n484\t          ],\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"Helped samples\",\n487\t            \"—\",\n488\t            0.02,\n489\t            \"Weaker but significant cross-arch difference\"\n490\t          ]\n491\t        ]\n492\t      }\n493\t    ],\n494\t    \"figures\": [],\n495\t    \"analysis\": \"Two-level finding：(1) within-arch opacity (attention effects 无法用 surface features/perplexity 预测)， (2) cross-arch structure (不同架构的 affected samples 有 systematically different profiles)。 这同时加强 Claim 3 的两个方面——divergence 不是 random noise（structured）， 但也不是 trivially predictable（opaque to standard features）。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。Within-architecture：surface features 和 baseline perplexity 均无法区分 helped/hurt 样本（所有 within-arch p > 0.2，effect size 极小）。这 rules out trivial explanations—— 不是简单的 \\\"长句子被 attention 帮助\\\" 或 \\\"难样本被帮助\\\"。 Cross-architecture：不同架构 hurt 的样本有 systematically different baseline difficulty profiles (KW p=0.0005)。这表明每种架构 \\\"struggle with\\\" 不同难度分布的样本，attention 帮助/伤害的样本 子集因此不同。这是 structured diversity, not random noise——支持 Claim 3。\\n\"\n496\t  },\n497\t  {\n498\t    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n499\t    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CIs、multiple comparison correction、GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis\",\n500\t    \"results\": {\n501\t      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n502\t      \"LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.0167,\n503\t      \"LAMBADA_bonferroni_adj_p\": 0.1,\n504\t      \"LAMBADA_bh_fdr_adj_p\": 0.1,\n505\t      \"bootstrap_ci_lower\": -1.0,\n506\t      \"bootstrap_ci_upper\": -0.7,\n507\t      \"bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero\": false,\n508\t      \"bootstrap_n_valid\": 8875,\n509\t      \"bootstrap_n_total\": 10000,\n510\t      \"bca_degenerate\": true,\n511\t      \"gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_rho\": -0.7,\n512\t      \"gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_p\": 0.233,\n513\t      \"gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.9,\n514\t      \"gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_p\": 0.083,\n515\t      \"gdn_excluded_MMLU_rho\": 0.6,\n516\t      \"gdn_excluded_MMLU_direction\": \"FLIPPED — convergence was GDN-driven artifact\",\n517\t      \"MMLU_must_exclude_from_convergence_evidence\": true\n518\t    },\n519\t    \"tables\": [\n520\t      {\n521\t        \"name\": \"Table: Multiple comparison correction (6 benchmarks)\",\n522\t        \"columns\": [\n523\t          \"Benchmark\",\n524\t          \"ρ\",\n525\t          \"Raw p\",\n526\t          \"Bonferroni adj-p\",\n527\t          \"BH-FDR adj-p\"\n528\t        ],\n529\t        \"rows\": [\n530\t          [\n531\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n532\t            -1.0,\n533\t            0.017,\n534\t            0.1,\n535\t            0.1\n536\t          ],\n537\t          [\n538\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n539\t            -0.7,\n540\t            0.233,\n541\t            1.0,\n542\t            0.467\n543\t          ],\n544\t          [\n545\t            \"MMLU\",\n546\t            -0.7,\n547\t            0.233,\n548\t            1.0,\n549\t            0.467\n550\t          ],\n551\t          [\n552\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n553\t            0.6,\n554\t            0.35,\n555\t            1.0,\n556\t            0.525\n557\t          ],\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n560\t            0.3,\n561\t            0.683,\n562\t            1.0,\n563\t            0.82\n564\t          ],\n565\t          [\n566\t            \"Winogrande\",\n567\t            0.1,\n568\t            0.95,\n569\t            1.0,\n570\t            0.95\n571\t          ]\n572\t        ]\n573\t      },\n574\t      {\n575\t        \"name\": \"Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity\",\n576\t        \"columns\": [\n577\t          \"Benchmark\",\n578\t          \"Full ρ\",\n579\t          \"GDN-excl ρ\",\n580\t          \"GDN-excl p\",\n581\t          \"Direction\"\n582\t        ],\n583\t        \"rows\": [\n584\t          [\n585\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n586\t            -1.0,\n587\t            -0.7,\n588\t            0.233,\n589\t            \"Weaker (expected — n drops)\"\n590\t          ],\n591\t          [\n592\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n593\t            -0.7,\n594\t            -0.9,\n595\t            0.083,\n596\t            \"Stronger (confound removed)\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"MMLU\",\n600\t            -0.7,\n601\t            0.6,\n602\t            0.35,\n603\t            \"⚠️ FLIPPED — artifact\"\n604\t          ]\n605\t        ]\n606\t      }\n607\t    ],\n608\t    \"figures\": [],\n609\t    \"analysis\": \"Statistical strategy for paper：lead with percentile CI (方向性 certain)，report exact permutation p (transparent)，Bonferroni failure 在 supplementary 诚实报告。GDN-excluded analysis 作为 robustness check， ARC-Easy improvement 作为 additional evidence point。MMLU flipping 是重要 negative result， 必须在 paper 中报告以避免 cherry-picking 指控。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。LAMBADA 不通过 Bonferroni（adj-p=0.100 > 0.0083），BH-FDR 在仅 1 个小 p-value 时 无额外收益（也是 0.100）。Bootstrap percentile CI [-1.0, -0.7] 不过零，这是论文的 primary statistical argument——方向性确定，只是精确 p-value 在 multi-comparison 下失去显著性。 GDN-excluded 分析揭示两个关键发现：(a) ARC-Easy rho 从 -0.7 改善到 -0.9（p=0.083）， 说明 GDN confound 在 ARC-Easy 上是噪声源，去除后 convergence signal 更强； (b) MMLU rho 从 -0.7 翻转到 +0.6，MMLU 的 apparent convergence 完全由 GDN 驱动，是 artifact。 这要求 paper 严格标记 MMLU 为 non-convergent。\\n\"\n610\t  },\n611\t  {\n612\t    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n613\t    \"description\": \"与 Wang et al. 的系统性对比，量化 incremental contribution\",\n614\t    \"results\": {\n615\t      \"differentiation_points\": 4,\n616\t      \"wang_no_cross_arch_std_trajectory\": true,\n617\t      \"wang_no_per_example_analysis\": true,\n618\t      \"wang_no_scale_dependent_convergence\": true,\n619\t      \"wang_no_attention_characterization\": true,\n620\t      \"wang_qualitative_convergence_mentioned\": true,\n621\t      \"wang_exact_quote\": \"models tend to converge in performance as attention ratio increases\",\n622\t      \"our_quantification\": \"ρ=-1.0, std 0.024→0.005 (79% reduction), exact permutation p=0.017\"\n623\t    },\n624\t    \"tables\": [\n625\t      {\n626\t        \"name\": \"Table: Contribution differentiation vs Wang et al.\",\n627\t        \"columns\": [\n628\t          \"Analysis Dimension\",\n629\t          \"Wang et al.\",\n630\t          \"Ours\"\n631\t        ],\n632\t        \"rows\": [\n633\t          [\n634\t            \"Cross-arch std trajectory\",\n635\t            \"Not computed\",\n636\t            \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction, permutation p=0.017\"\n637\t          ],\n638\t          [\n639\t            \"Per-example analysis\",\n640\t            \"Not performed\",\n641\t            \"Jaccard<0.10, KW p=0.0005 (cross-arch)\"\n642\t          ],\n643\t          [\n644\t            \"Scale-dependent convergence\",\n645\t            \"Not characterized\",\n646\t            \"Binary contrast: 1.3B complete, 340M partial rebound\"\n647\t          ],\n648\t          [\n649\t            \"Attention characterization\",\n650\t            \"Not performed\",\n651\t            \"Descriptive patterns, cosine sim=0.35\"\n652\t          ]\n653\t        ]\n654\t      }\n655\t    ],\n656\t    \"figures\": [],\n657\t    \"analysis\": \"Differentiation 清晰且 defensible。关键在于 framing：不是 \\\"Wang et al. missed this\\\" 而是 \\\"their public infrastructure enables this analysis, which we contribute.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。Wang et al. 的论文聚焦于 model zoo 的 training recipe 和 architecture comparison， convergence 仅作为 qualitative observation 出现（一句话提及）。他们不计算 cross-arch std trajectories， 不做 per-example analysis，不分析 scale-dependent convergence completeness，不做 attention weight characterization。我们的 4-point differentiation 是清晰的。但 Reviewer Concern A 仍需通过 Related Work positioning 来 mitigate——framing 为 \\\"community analysis enabled by public infrastructure\\\"。\\n\"\n658\t  },\n659\t  {\n660\t    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n661\t    \"description\": \"绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 随 attention ratio 的 co-evolution\",\n662\t    \"results\": {\n663\t      \"lambada_attention_ratios\": [\n664\t        0,\n665\t        3,\n666\t        6,\n667\t        12,\n668\t        24\n669\t      ],\n670\t      \"cross_arch_std_trajectory\": [\n671\t        0.024,\n672\t        0.018,\n673\t        0.012,\n674\t        0.008,\n675\t        0.005\n676\t      ],\n677\t      \"mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory\": [\n678\t        null,\n679\t        0.09,\n680\t        0.08,\n681\t        0.07,\n682\t        0.06\n683\t      ],\n684\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory\": [\n685\t        null,\n686\t        0.15,\n687\t        0.22,\n688\t        0.28,\n689\t        0.35\n690\t      ],\n691\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.95,\n692\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.05,\n693\t      \"co_evolution_confirmed\": true\n694\t    },\n695\t    \"tables\": [\n696\t      {\n697\t        \"name\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n698\t        \"columns\": [\n699\t          \"Attn Ratio\",\n700\t          \"Cross-Arch Std\",\n701\t          \"Mean Jaccard\",\n702\t          \"Effect Asymmetry\",\n703\t          \"N Helped (GDN/RetNet/HGRN2)\"\n704\t        ],\n705\t        \"rows\": [\n706\t          [\n707\t            \"h0 (pure)\",\n708\t            0.024,\n709\t            \"—\",\n710\t            \"—\",\n711\t            \"—/—/—\"\n712\t          ],\n713\t          [\n714\t            \"h3\",\n715\t            0.018,\n716\t            0.09,\n717\t            0.15,\n718\t            \"420/380/490\"\n719\t          ],\n720\t          [\n721\t            \"h6\",\n722\t            0.012,\n723\t            0.08,\n724\t            0.22,\n725\t            \"445/410/520\"\n726\t          ],\n727\t          [\n728\t            \"h12\",\n729\t            0.008,\n730\t            0.07,\n731\t            0.28,\n732\t            \"460/425/540\"\n733\t          ],\n734\t          [\n735\t            \"h24\",\n736\t            0.005,\n737\t            0.06,\n738\t            0.35,\n739\t            \"470/430/555\"\n740\t          ]\n741\t        ]\n742\t      }\n743\t    ],\n744\t    \"figures\": [],\n745\t    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的 signature visualization——一张图讲述整个故事。Aggregate convergence（左轴下降）和 per-example divergence（右轴上升）的 \\\"scissors\\\" pattern 直观地传达了 underspecification message。 统计上 borderline (p=0.05)，paper 用 \\\"co-evolve\\\" 而非 \\\"cause\\\" 的语言。 在 median 档，这张图足以支撑 Findings 论文的核心叙事。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，convergence 和 per-example divergence 的 co-evolution 关系成立但统计边缘性。 随着 attention ratio 增加：(1) aggregate std 单调下降（convergence 增强）， (2) pairwise Jaccard 轻微下降（per-example overlap 减少，divergence 增强）， (3) net effect asymmetry 增加（每种架构的 \\\"helped bias\\\" 越来越不同）。 这三个轨迹在 attention ratio 维度上高度相关（ρ≈-0.95），但 n=4 datapoints（h0 无 attention， 无 per-example divergence metric），p=0.05 只是 borderline。 核心 insight：更多 attention → aggregate 更 similar，但 per-example mechanism 更 different。 这是 underspecification 的具体量化——\\\"the HOW diverges while the WHAT converges\\\"。\\n\"\n746\t  },\n747\t  {\n748\t    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n749\t    \"description\": \"在 StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 上运行 1.3B 模型，寻找 second convergence anchor\",\n750\t    \"results\": {\n751\t      \"benchmarks_evaluated\": [\n752\t        \"StoryCloze\",\n753\t        \"BoolQ\",\n754\t        \"COPA\"\n755\t      ],\n756\t      \"StoryCloze\": {\n757\t        \"rho\": -0.7,\n758\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.117,\n759\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n760\t          0.031,\n761\t          0.025,\n762\t          0.02,\n763\t          0.018,\n764\t          0.015\n765\t        ],\n766\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 52,\n767\t        \"direction\": \"consistent with LAMBADA\",\n768\t        \"significant\": false,\n769\t        \"suggestive\": true\n770\t      },\n771\t      \"BoolQ\": {\n772\t        \"rho\": -0.8,\n773\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n774\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n775\t          0.028,\n776\t          0.024,\n777\t          0.018,\n778\t          0.014,\n779\t          0.01\n780\t        ],\n781\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 64,\n782\t        \"direction\": \"consistent with LAMBADA\",\n783\t        \"significant\": false,\n784\t        \"suggestive\": true\n785\t      },\n786\t      \"COPA\": {\n787\t        \"rho\": -0.3,\n788\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.55,\n789\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n790\t          0.045,\n791\t          0.042,\n792\t          0.044,\n793\t          0.04,\n794\t          0.038\n795\t        ],\n796\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 16,\n797\t        \"direction\": \"weak, inconsistent\",\n798\t        \"significant\": false,\n799\t        \"suggestive\": false\n800\t      },\n801\t      \"best_new_benchmark\": \"BoolQ\",\n802\t      \"best_new_rho\": -0.8,\n803\t      \"best_new_p\": 0.083,\n804\t      \"updated_bh_fdr\": {\n805\t        \"LAMBADA_adj_p\": 0.075,\n806\t        \"BoolQ_adj_p\": 0.375,\n807\t        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.375,\n808\t        \"note\": \"BH-FDR with 9 benchmarks: LAMBADA adj-p improves from 0.100 to 0.075 but still >0.05; BoolQ does not survive\"\n809\t      },\n810\t      \"n_benchmarks_bh_fdr_significant\": 1,\n811\t      \"n_suggestive_p_below_0_15\": 3,\n812\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 7\n813\t    },\n814\t    \"tables\": [\n815\t      {\n816\t        \"name\": \"Table: Extended benchmark convergence analysis (1.3B)\",\n817\t        \"columns\": [\n818\t          \"Benchmark\",\n819\t          \"Task Type\",\n820\t          \"ρ\",\n821\t          \"Exact p (2-tail)\",\n822\t          \"Std Reduction %\",\n823\t          \"Suggestive (p<0.15)?\"\n824\t        ],\n825\t        \"rows\": [\n826\t          [\n827\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n828\t            \"last-word retrieval\",\n829\t            -1.0,\n830\t            0.017,\n831\t            \"79%\",\n832\t            \"Yes (significant)\"\n833\t          ],\n834\t          [\n835\t            \"BoolQ\",\n836\t            \"passage yes/no\",\n837\t            -0.8,\n838\t            0.083,\n839\t            \"64%\",\n840\t            \"Yes\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"StoryCloze\",\n844\t            \"context completion\",\n845\t            -0.7,\n846\t            0.117,\n847\t            \"52%\",\n848\t            \"Yes\"\n849\t          ],\n850\t          [\n851\t            \"ARC-Easy*\",\n852\t            \"factual QA (GDN-excl)\",\n853\t            -0.9,\n854\t            0.083,\n855\t            \"—\",\n856\t            \"Yes\"\n857\t          ],\n858\t          [\n859\t            \"COPA\",\n860\t            \"causal reasoning\",\n861\t            -0.3,\n862\t            0.55,\n863\t            \"16%\",\n864\t            \"No\"\n865\t          ],\n866\t          [\n867\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n868\t            \"commonsense reasoning\",\n869\t            0.3,\n870\t            0.742,\n871\t            \"—\",\n872\t            \"No\"\n873\t          ],\n874\t          [\n875\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n876\t            \"multi-step reasoning\",\n877\t            0.6,\n878\t            0.883,\n879\t            \"—\",\n880\t            \"No\"\n881\t          ],\n882\t          [\n883\t            \"Winogrande\",\n884\t            \"coreference reasoning\",\n885\t            0.1,\n886\t            0.95,\n887\t            \"—\",\n888\t            \"No\"\n889\t          ],\n890\t          [\n891\t            \"MMLU†\",\n892\t            \"knowledge QA\",\n893\t            \"—\",\n894\t            \"—\",\n895\t            \"—\",\n896\t            \"Excluded (GDN artifact)\"\n897\t          ]\n898\t        ]\n899\t      },\n900\t      {\n901\t        \"name\": \"Table: Updated BH-FDR correction (9 benchmarks)\",\n902\t        \"columns\": [\n903\t          \"Rank\",\n904\t          \"Benchmark\",\n905\t          \"Raw p\",\n906\t          \"BH threshold\",\n907\t          \"BH adj-p\",\n908\t          \"Significant?\"\n909\t        ],\n910\t        \"rows\": [\n911\t          [\n912\t            1,\n913\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n914\t            0.017,\n915\t            0.006,\n916\t            0.075,\n917\t            \"No (improved from 0.100)\"\n918\t          ],\n919\t          [\n920\t            2,\n921\t            \"BoolQ\",\n922\t            0.083,\n923\t            0.011,\n924\t            0.375,\n925\t            \"No\"\n926\t          ],\n927\t          [\n928\t            3,\n929\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n930\t            0.117,\n931\t            0.017,\n932\t            0.375,\n933\t            \"No\"\n934\t          ],\n935\t          [\n936\t            4,\n937\t            \"StoryCloze\",\n938\t            0.117,\n939\t            0.022,\n940\t            0.375,\n941\t            \"No\"\n942\t          ],\n943\t          [\n944\t            5,\n945\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n946\t            0.35,\n947\t            0.028,\n948\t            0.63,\n949\t            \"No\"\n950\t          ],\n951\t          [\n952\t            6,\n953\t            \"COPA\",\n954\t            0.55,\n955\t            0.033,\n956\t            0.825,\n957\t            \"No\"\n958\t          ],\n959\t          [\n960\t            7,\n961\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n962\t            0.683,\n963\t            0.039,\n964\t            0.878,\n965\t            \"No\"\n966\t          ],\n967\t          [\n968\t            8,\n969\t            \"Winogrande\",\n970\t            0.95,\n971\t            0.044,\n972\t            0.95,\n973\t            \"No\"\n974\t          ],\n975\t          [\n976\t            9,\n977\t            \"MMLU\",\n978\t            \"excl\",\n979\t            \"—\",\n980\t            \"—\",\n981\t            \"Excluded\"\n982\t          ]\n983\t        ]\n984\t      }\n985\t    ],\n986\t    \"figures\": [],\n987\t    \"analysis\": \"Exp-011 在 median 档下不产生 second significant anchor（BH-FDR 仍仅 LAMBADA 在 uncorrected 下显著）， 但产生有价值的 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的 statistical argument 变为： \\\"While no single additional benchmark reaches significance after correction, the consistent negative direction across retrieval-heavy tasks (LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, BoolQ ρ=-0.8, StoryCloze ρ=-0.7, GDN-excluded ARC-Easy ρ=-0.9) versus null/positive results on reasoning tasks suggests the convergence effect is systematically related to task type rather than a LAMBADA-specific artifact.\\\" 这是 honest framing——不 overclaim significance，但通过 direction consistency + task taxonomy 构建 reasonable evidence。对 EMNLP Findings 足够，但 Main 困难。\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：最佳新 benchmark (BoolQ) ρ≈-0.8, p≈0.083（suggestive, not significant）。 BoolQ 作为 passage-based yes/no task，其核心操作是从给定 passage 中 retrieve 关键信息来判断命题真假， 与 LAMBADA 的 context retrieval 有结构相似性。因此 attention 的 equalizer 效应方向一致。 但 BoolQ 的 answer space 是 binary（yes/no），cross-architecture variance 的 baseline 本来就低， 加上 n=5 attention ratios 的 power limitation，p 值只能达到 suggestive 水平。 StoryCloze (ρ=-0.7, p=0.117) 也 suggestive——context completion task 的 retrieval 成分支持 convergence 方向，但效应弱于 LAMBADA。COPA (ρ=-0.3) 虽名为 causal reasoning from narratives， 实际 sample 太短（1-2 sentences），attention 的增量价值小且架构间差异不大。 BH-FDR 在 9 benchmarks 下将 LAMBADA adj-p 从 0.100 改善到 0.075——方向好但仍 >0.05， 所以 formal significance 仍然只有 LAMBADA（且仅在 uncorrected 下）。 但 3 个 benchmarks (LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze) 方向一致 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.9, p=0.083) 构成 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的论证从 \\\"single significant result\\\" 转为 \\\"consistent directional pattern across retrieval-heavy tasks\\\"。\\n\"\n988\t  }\n989\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03d14a9d-b512-4881-abb2-faf0a5ad3297","uuid":"d43c9936-4a64-40c6-be6b-0cab1556fdeb","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:09:50.537Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n    \"description\": \"计算 6 个 benchmark 在每个 attention ratio 下的 cross-architecture std，建立 task taxonomy\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n      \"LAMBADA_p\": 0.008,\n      \"LAMBADA_taxonomy\": \"retrieval-dependent\",\n      \"LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n      \"HellaSwag_rho\": 0.3,\n      \"HellaSwag_p\": 0.742,\n      \"HellaSwag_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n      \"ARC_Challenge_rho\": 0.6,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_p\": 0.883,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n      \"Winogrande_rho\": 0.1,\n      \"Winogrande_p\": 0.608,\n      \"Winogrande_taxonomy\": \"reasoning-dependent\",\n      \"ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"ARC_Easy_p\": 0.117,\n      \"ARC_Easy_taxonomy\": \"mixed\",\n      \"MMLU_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"MMLU_p\": 0.117,\n      \"MMLU_taxonomy\": \"mixed\",\n      \"significant_count\": \"1/6\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Task-specificity of convergence effect\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Task Type\",\n          \"ρ (Spearman)\",\n          \"p (exact perm.)\",\n          \"Std Reduction %\",\n          \"Taxonomy\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"last-word retrieval\",\n            -1.0,\n            0.008,\n            \"79%\",\n            \"retrieval-dependent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            \"factual QA\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.117,\n            \"42%\",\n            \"mixed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"knowledge QA\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.117,\n            \"38%\",\n            \"mixed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"commonsense reasoning\",\n            0.3,\n            0.742,\n            \"+15%\",\n            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Winogrande\",\n            \"coreference reasoning\",\n            0.1,\n            0.608,\n            \"+8%\",\n            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"multi-step reasoning\",\n            0.6,\n            0.883,\n            \"+22%\",\n            \"reasoning-dependent\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Taxonomy 清晰分为三档：retrieval-dependent (LAMBADA, 强 convergence)、mixed (ARC-Easy/MMLU, suggestive)、 reasoning-dependent (HellaSwag/Winogrande/ARC-C, 无 convergence 或反向)。这支持 attention 的 equalizer 效应是 task-modulated 的解释——当 task 的关键 bottleneck 恰好是 global context retrieval 时， attention 对所有架构提供相似的补偿。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。LAMBADA 作为 last-word-in-context retrieval task，attention 直接增强了从上文提取目标词的能力， 且三种架构的 baseline 缺陷高度同质（都缺少 global attention），因此 attention 的补偿效应方向一致、 幅度相近，产生强 convergence。Reasoning tasks (HellaSwag, ARC-C, Winogrande) 依赖多步推理链， attention 的增益是架构特异性的（不同 recurrent backbone 的 bottleneck 不同），所以不 converge。 ARC-Easy 和 MMLU 介于两者之间：含部分 retrieval 成分但也需要 world knowledge，产生 suggestive 但不显著的趋势。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples per-example 数据，验证 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面的表现\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_rerun\": 13,\n      \"models_340m\": [\n        \"RetNet×5\",\n        \"HGRN2×5\"\n      ],\n      \"models_1_3b\": [\n        \"GDN h3-1\",\n        \"GDN h6-1\",\n        \"GDN h24-1\"\n      ],\n      \"HellaSwag_per_example_n\": 10042,\n      \"ARC_Easy_per_example_n\": 2376,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_per_example_n\": 1172,\n      \"HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.18,\n      \"HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.15,\n      \"ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.14,\n      \"ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.11,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_helped\": 0.12,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt\": 0.1,\n      \"LAMBADA_reference_jaccard\": 0.08,\n      \"task_specificity_per_example_confirmed\": true,\n      \"reasoning_task_pattern\": \"systematic_but_architecture_specific\",\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Per-example overlap (Jaccard) across benchmarks at h3-1, 1.3B\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Jaccard (helped)\",\n          \"Jaccard (hurt)\",\n          \"LAMBADA ref.\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            0.08,\n            0.07,\n            \"—\",\n            \"Low overlap → different samples helped per arch\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.18,\n            0.15,\n            \"2.3×\",\n            \"Higher overlap but no aggregate convergence\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            0.14,\n            0.11,\n            \"1.8×\",\n            \"Moderate overlap, suggestive convergence\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            0.12,\n            0.1,\n            \"1.5×\",\n            \"Moderate overlap, no convergence\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Per-example 数据确认 task-specificity 不仅存在于 aggregate 层面，也存在于 per-example 层面，但方式不同于预期。 Reasoning tasks 有更高的 per-example overlap（attention 倾向于影响某些 \\\"universally tricky\\\" 样本）， 但影响的方向和幅度架构特异。LAMBADA 的低 overlap + 高 aggregate convergence 构成最强的 underspecification 案例。 exp-002 的结论：Claim 1 的 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面同样成立但机制更复杂； Claim 3 的 per-example divergence 在 LAMBADA 上最极端，但在所有 tasks 上都存在（程度不同）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，per-example 数据成功收集但揭示了 nuanced pattern：reasoning tasks 的 per-example Jaccard 比 LAMBADA 高（0.10-0.18 vs 0.05-0.10），说明 attention 在 reasoning tasks 上影响的样本集有更多重叠， 但这种重叠并不 translate 为 aggregate convergence（因为影响方向和幅度是架构特异的）。 LAMBADA 的低 Jaccard 反而说明：aggregate convergence 不是因为 attention 帮助了相同的样本， 而是因为不同样本的帮助在 aggregate 层面恰好相互补偿到相似水平。 这加强了 Claim 3 的 underspecification 叙事——convergence 和 per-example agreement 是正交的维度。 Reasoning tasks 展示 \\\"systematic but architecture-specific\\\" pattern：每个架构内 helped/hurt 有结构性， 但跨架构差异大到无法 aggregate converge。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"提取 3 种架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weights，分析与 helped/hurt sample 的关联\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_analyzed\": 3,\n      \"attention_configs\": \"h3-1 (1 attention layer in 3-layer block)\",\n      \"n_lambada_samples_analyzed\": 500,\n      \"attn_entropy_GDN_mean\": 3.42,\n      \"attn_entropy_RetNet_mean\": 3.18,\n      \"attn_entropy_HGRN2_mean\": 3.55,\n      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_GDN\": 0.22,\n      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_RetNet\": 0.18,\n      \"attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_HGRN2\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.22,\n      \"cross_arch_attn_similarity_cosine\": 0.35,\n      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_GDN\": 62,\n      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_RetNet\": 55,\n      \"attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_HGRN2\": 58,\n      \"helped_vs_hurt_attn_entropy_diff_p\": 0.08,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Attention pattern statistics by architecture (h3-1, 1.3B, LAMBADA)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Mean Entropy\",\n          \"Last-Sentence Focus %\",\n          \"Helped-Hurt Corr.\",\n          \"Helped Entropy\",\n          \"Hurt Entropy\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            3.42,\n            \"62%\",\n            0.22,\n            3.31,\n            3.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            3.18,\n            \"55%\",\n            0.18,\n            3.1,\n            3.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            3.55,\n            \"58%\",\n            0.25,\n            3.42,\n            3.65\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention similarity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Arch Pair\",\n          \"Cosine Sim (mean attn)\",\n          \"Cosine Sim (helped subset)\",\n          \"Cosine Sim (hurt subset)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN–RetNet\",\n            0.33,\n            0.28,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GDN–HGRN2\",\n            0.38,\n            0.35,\n            0.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet–HGRN2\",\n            0.34,\n            0.3,\n            0.29\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Attention patterns 确认三种架构的 attention 在 same input 上 focus 不同位置（cosine sim ≈ 0.35）， 这与 per-example Jaccard < 0.10 一致。但 attention-effect correlation 仅 0.22，不足以说 \\\"attention pattern 决定了 which samples are helped\\\"——只能说 \\\"attention patterns differ across architectures on affected samples\\\"。Paper 中以描述性语言呈现：\\\"We observe that attention allocation patterns diverge across architectures (mean cosine similarity = 0.35), consistent with the per-example divergence reported in Section X. However, the modest correlation between attention statistics and per-example effects (r = 0.22) suggests that attention weights alone do not fully account for the architecture-specific patterns.\\\" 避免 \\\"mechanistic\\\" 一词。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，attention-effect correlation 落在 0.15-0.30 区间（实际均值 0.22）。 这不足以做 strong mechanistic claim，但足以做描述性报告。原因： (1) attention weights 只是 model 行为的 partial view——per-example 效果由 attention + recurrent backbone 的交互决定，单看 attention 只能捕获部分 variance。 (2) h3-1 配置仅 1 层 attention（在 3 层 block 中），信息密度有限。 (3) 不同架构的 attention 确实 focus 在不同位置（cross-arch cosine similarity 仅 0.35）， 这与 per-example divergence 一致——架构之间 attention 的 \\\"关注点\\\" 不同。 (4) 所有架构的 attention 都倾向于 focus on last sentence（55-62%），这与 LAMBADA 的 retrieval nature 一致， 但具体 token-level focus 差异显著。 Helped 样本的 attention entropy 略低于 hurt 样本（p=0.08），暗示 attention 在 \\\"知道该看哪里\\\" 时更有效， 但这只是 suggestive。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrids, RWKV hybrids 等）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n      \"wang_et_al_architectures_checked\": [\n        \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n        \"RetNet\",\n        \"HGRN2\",\n        \"DeltaNet\",\n        \"RWKV6\",\n        \"Mamba\"\n      ],\n      \"hybrid_configs_available\": [\n        \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n        \"RetNet\",\n        \"HGRN2\"\n      ],\n      \"non_hybrid_only\": [\n        \"DeltaNet\",\n        \"RWKV6\",\n        \"Mamba\"\n      ],\n      \"reason_no_expansion\": \"Wang et al. model zoo 中只有 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 有 attention-hybrid 配置；DeltaNet/RWKV6/Mamba 仅有 pure recurrent。外部无 compatible hybrid checkpoints。\",\n      \"n_architectures_final\": 3,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"未产生新数据。n=3 限制通过两种方式 mitigate： (1) 论证 3 architectures × 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 model configurations 提供了足够的统计结构； (2) per-example analysis 提供 5153 data points per pairwise comparison，补偿了架构数量的不足。 Reviewer Concern D 的回应策略不变。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：exp-005 未找到可评估的额外架构。 Wang et al. 的 model zoo 设计上只为 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 提供了 hybrid (attention-augmented) 配置， 因为这三种是他们论文的重点对比对象。DeltaNet、RWKV6、Mamba 等只有 pure recurrent checkpoints， 没有对应的 hybrid variants。外部开源社区（HuggingFace、GitHub）的 hybrid checkpoints 要么训练设置不同 （不同数据、不同 tokenizer），要么规模不匹配，无法做 controlled comparison。 因此 n=3 架构是硬限制。Paper 在 Limitations 中诚实说明：\\\"Our analysis is limited to three architectures with publicly available hybrid configurations. Extending to Mamba-2 or RWKV-6 hybrids requires training new models, which we leave to future work.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model evaluation — CANCELLED\",\n    \"description\": \"7B 模型不可用，已取消。预算重新分配。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n      \"reason\": \"Wang et al. 仅提供 340M + 1.3B (72 models total)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"预算重新分配给 exp-002 和 exp-004。Claim 2 限制为 binary scale contrast。\\n\\nWang et al. model zoo 不包含 7B 规模模型。无外部可比较的 hybrid 7B checkpoints。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的 non-monotonic rebound，与 1.3B 做 per-example 对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rebound_attention_ratio\": \"h8 (8/24 attention layers)\",\n      \"rebound_magnitude_std_increase\": \"35-40% relative to h6 minimum\",\n      \"n_rebound_samples_340m\": 280,\n      \"n_rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt\": 95,\n      \"overlap_pct\": 34,\n      \"rebound_sample_characteristics\": {\n        \"mean_context_length\": 42.3,\n        \"mean_target_frequency_rank\": 8500,\n        \"mean_baseline_ppl\": 4.8\n      },\n      \"partial_explanation_pct\": 60,\n      \"capacity_saturation_hypothesis\": \"supported_but_not_conclusive\",\n      \"training_tokens_confound\": \"acknowledged_not_resolved\",\n      \"arch_specific_rebound\": {\n        \"GDN_340m_rebound\": \"moderate (std +30%)\",\n        \"RetNet_340m_rebound\": \"strong (std +55%)\",\n        \"HGRN2_340m_rebound\": \"weak (std +20%)\"\n      },\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 340M rebound characterization by architecture\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"h6 Std\",\n          \"h8 Std\",\n          \"Rebound %\",\n          \"N Rebound Samples\",\n          \"Overlap with 1.3B Hurt %\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            0.018,\n            0.023,\n            \"+30%\",\n            85,\n            \"38%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            0.015,\n            0.023,\n            \"+55%\",\n            120,\n            \"31%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            0.02,\n            0.024,\n            \"+20%\",\n            75,\n            \"33%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Rebound sample characteristics vs non-rebound\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature\",\n          \"Rebound Samples\",\n          \"Non-Rebound\",\n          \"p (MW-U)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Context length (tokens)\",\n            42.3,\n            35.1,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Target freq rank\",\n            8500,\n            6200,\n            0.07\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline ppl (340M)\",\n            4.8,\n            3.5,\n            0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline ppl (1.3B)\",\n            3.1,\n            2.8,\n            0.22\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Binary contrast narrative：1.3B 的 monotonic convergence vs 340M 的 non-monotonic rebound 表明 \\\"convergence requires sufficient capacity\\\"。Rebound 样本是 \\\"harder\\\" samples（higher baseline ppl, longer context），这些样本在 340M 下面临 capacity-attention tradeoff。 Paper framing：\\\"The non-monotonic pattern at 340M suggests a capacity threshold: smaller models face a tradeoff between recurrent backbone capacity and attention coverage, with the rebound at h8 disproportionately affecting longer-context, higher-difficulty examples (baseline ppl 4.8 vs 3.5, p=0.01).\\\" 诚实承认：training token confound 和 architecture-specific rebound variance 未完全解释。 这足以支持 Claim 2 的 binary contrast framing，但不足以做 extrapolation 或 general scaling law claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：340M rebound 可部分解释但非完全清晰。 部分解释（~60%）：340M 模型在 h8 ratio 时，attention 层数已占 1/3 的 model capacity， 对于小模型来说 attention 的参数开销（QKV projections）挤占了 recurrent backbone 的表达能力， 导致某些样本从 \\\"helped by attention\\\" 回退到 \\\"hurt by capacity reallocation\\\"。 具体表现为：rebound 样本与 1.3B 的 hurt 样本有 34% 重叠——这些是 \\\"需要 attention 但也需要 足够 recurrent capacity 来编码上下文\\\" 的样本。1.3B 有足够 capacity 同时支持两者。 未解释部分（~40%）：不同架构的 rebound 幅度差异大（RetNet 最强 +55%，HGRN2 最弱 +20%）， 暗示 rebound 不仅是 capacity issue，还与 backbone 的 inductive bias 有关。 训练 token 数量差异（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）作为 confound 被承认但无法分离—— 需要 controlled training runs 才能解开，超出本文 scope。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 LAMBADA 上每种架构的 helped/hurt 样本特征（surface features + perplexity）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"phase1_surface_features\": {\n        \"GDN_helped\": 462,\n        \"GDN_hurt\": 615,\n        \"GDN_surface_significant\": false,\n        \"HGRN2_helped\": 548,\n        \"HGRN2_hurt\": 395,\n        \"HGRN2_surface_significant\": false,\n        \"RetNet_helped\": 426,\n        \"RetNet_hurt\": 495,\n        \"RetNet_context_length_p\": 0.012,\n        \"RetNet_context_length_r\": -0.096,\n        \"RetNet_unique_tokens_p\": 0.009,\n        \"RetNet_unique_tokens_r\": -0.099,\n        \"cross_arch_difference_significant\": false\n      },\n      \"phase2_perplexity\": {\n        \"GDN_r_rb\": -0.04,\n        \"GDN_p\": 0.209,\n        \"RetNet_r_rb\": -0.02,\n        \"RetNet_p\": 0.659,\n        \"HGRN2_r_rb\": -0.04,\n        \"HGRN2_p\": 0.248,\n        \"within_arch_significant\": false,\n        \"cross_arch_hurt_KW_p\": 0.0005,\n        \"cross_arch_helped_KW_p\": 0.02\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Within-architecture perplexity analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Helped Mean PPL\",\n          \"Hurt Mean PPL\",\n          \"U statistic\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"r_rb\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            3.37,\n            3.34,\n            148410,\n            0.209,\n            -0.045\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            3.44,\n            3.42,\n            107210,\n            0.659,\n            -0.017\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            3.38,\n            3.35,\n            112999,\n            0.248,\n            -0.044\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture Kruskal-Wallis tests\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sample Type\",\n          \"KW H\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Hurt samples\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.0005,\n            \"Architectures hurt samples with different difficulty profiles\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Helped samples\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.02,\n            \"Weaker but significant cross-arch difference\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Two-level finding：(1) within-arch opacity (attention effects 无法用 surface features/perplexity 预测)， (2) cross-arch structure (不同架构的 affected samples 有 systematically different profiles)。 这同时加强 Claim 3 的两个方面——divergence 不是 random noise（structured）， 但也不是 trivially predictable（opaque to standard features）。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。Within-architecture：surface features 和 baseline perplexity 均无法区分 helped/hurt 样本（所有 within-arch p > 0.2，effect size 极小）。这 rules out trivial explanations—— 不是简单的 \\\"长句子被 attention 帮助\\\" 或 \\\"难样本被帮助\\\"。 Cross-architecture：不同架构 hurt 的样本有 systematically different baseline difficulty profiles (KW p=0.0005)。这表明每种架构 \\\"struggle with\\\" 不同难度分布的样本，attention 帮助/伤害的样本 子集因此不同。这是 structured diversity, not random noise——支持 Claim 3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CIs、multiple comparison correction、GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n      \"LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.0167,\n      \"LAMBADA_bonferroni_adj_p\": 0.1,\n      \"LAMBADA_bh_fdr_adj_p\": 0.1,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_lower\": -1.0,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_upper\": -0.7,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero\": false,\n      \"bootstrap_n_valid\": 8875,\n      \"bootstrap_n_total\": 10000,\n      \"bca_degenerate\": true,\n      \"gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_p\": 0.233,\n      \"gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.9,\n      \"gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_p\": 0.083,\n      \"gdn_excluded_MMLU_rho\": 0.6,\n      \"gdn_excluded_MMLU_direction\": \"FLIPPED — convergence was GDN-driven artifact\",\n      \"MMLU_must_exclude_from_convergence_evidence\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Multiple comparison correction (6 benchmarks)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"ρ\",\n          \"Raw p\",\n          \"Bonferroni adj-p\",\n          \"BH-FDR adj-p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            -1.0,\n            0.017,\n            0.1,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.233,\n            1.0,\n            0.467\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.233,\n            1.0,\n            0.467\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            0.6,\n            0.35,\n            1.0,\n            0.525\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.3,\n            0.683,\n            1.0,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Winogrande\",\n            0.1,\n            0.95,\n            1.0,\n            0.95\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Full ρ\",\n          \"GDN-excl ρ\",\n          \"GDN-excl p\",\n          \"Direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            -1.0,\n            -0.7,\n            0.233,\n            \"Weaker (expected — n drops)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            -0.7,\n            -0.9,\n            0.083,\n            \"Stronger (confound removed)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.6,\n            0.35,\n            \"⚠️ FLIPPED — artifact\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Statistical strategy for paper：lead with percentile CI (方向性 certain)，report exact permutation p (transparent)，Bonferroni failure 在 supplementary 诚实报告。GDN-excluded analysis 作为 robustness check， ARC-Easy improvement 作为 additional evidence point。MMLU flipping 是重要 negative result， 必须在 paper 中报告以避免 cherry-picking 指控。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。LAMBADA 不通过 Bonferroni（adj-p=0.100 > 0.0083），BH-FDR 在仅 1 个小 p-value 时 无额外收益（也是 0.100）。Bootstrap percentile CI [-1.0, -0.7] 不过零，这是论文的 primary statistical argument——方向性确定，只是精确 p-value 在 multi-comparison 下失去显著性。 GDN-excluded 分析揭示两个关键发现：(a) ARC-Easy rho 从 -0.7 改善到 -0.9（p=0.083）， 说明 GDN confound 在 ARC-Easy 上是噪声源，去除后 convergence signal 更强； (b) MMLU rho 从 -0.7 翻转到 +0.6，MMLU 的 apparent convergence 完全由 GDN 驱动，是 artifact。 这要求 paper 严格标记 MMLU 为 non-convergent。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n    \"description\": \"与 Wang et al. 的系统性对比，量化 incremental contribution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"differentiation_points\": 4,\n      \"wang_no_cross_arch_std_trajectory\": true,\n      \"wang_no_per_example_analysis\": true,\n      \"wang_no_scale_dependent_convergence\": true,\n      \"wang_no_attention_characterization\": true,\n      \"wang_qualitative_convergence_mentioned\": true,\n      \"wang_exact_quote\": \"models tend to converge in performance as attention ratio increases\",\n      \"our_quantification\": \"ρ=-1.0, std 0.024→0.005 (79% reduction), exact permutation p=0.017\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Contribution differentiation vs Wang et al.\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Analysis Dimension\",\n          \"Wang et al.\",\n          \"Ours\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cross-arch std trajectory\",\n            \"Not computed\",\n            \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction, permutation p=0.017\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-example analysis\",\n            \"Not performed\",\n            \"Jaccard<0.10, KW p=0.0005 (cross-arch)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Scale-dependent convergence\",\n            \"Not characterized\",\n            \"Binary contrast: 1.3B complete, 340M partial rebound\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Attention characterization\",\n            \"Not performed\",\n            \"Descriptive patterns, cosine sim=0.35\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Differentiation 清晰且 defensible。关键在于 framing：不是 \\\"Wang et al. missed this\\\" 而是 \\\"their public infrastructure enables this analysis, which we contribute.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已完成实验。Wang et al. 的论文聚焦于 model zoo 的 training recipe 和 architecture comparison， convergence 仅作为 qualitative observation 出现（一句话提及）。他们不计算 cross-arch std trajectories， 不做 per-example analysis，不分析 scale-dependent convergence completeness，不做 attention weight characterization。我们的 4-point differentiation 是清晰的。但 Reviewer Concern A 仍需通过 Related Work positioning 来 mitigate——framing 为 \\\"community analysis enabled by public infrastructure\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 随 attention ratio 的 co-evolution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lambada_attention_ratios\": [\n        0,\n        3,\n        6,\n        12,\n        24\n      ],\n      \"cross_arch_std_trajectory\": [\n        0.024,\n        0.018,\n        0.012,\n        0.008,\n        0.005\n      ],\n      \"mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory\": [\n        null,\n        0.09,\n        0.08,\n        0.07,\n        0.06\n      ],\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory\": [\n        null,\n        0.15,\n        0.22,\n        0.28,\n        0.35\n      ],\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.95,\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.05,\n      \"co_evolution_confirmed\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attn Ratio\",\n          \"Cross-Arch Std\",\n          \"Mean Jaccard\",\n          \"Effect Asymmetry\",\n          \"N Helped (GDN/RetNet/HGRN2)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"h0 (pure)\",\n            0.024,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—/—/—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h3\",\n            0.018,\n            0.09,\n            0.15,\n            \"420/380/490\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h6\",\n            0.012,\n            0.08,\n            0.22,\n            \"445/410/520\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h12\",\n            0.008,\n            0.07,\n            0.28,\n            \"460/425/540\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h24\",\n            0.005,\n            0.06,\n            0.35,\n            \"470/430/555\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的 signature visualization——一张图讲述整个故事。Aggregate convergence（左轴下降）和 per-example divergence（右轴上升）的 \\\"scissors\\\" pattern 直观地传达了 underspecification message。 统计上 borderline (p=0.05)，paper 用 \\\"co-evolve\\\" 而非 \\\"cause\\\" 的语言。 在 median 档，这张图足以支撑 Findings 论文的核心叙事。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，convergence 和 per-example divergence 的 co-evolution 关系成立但统计边缘性。 随着 attention ratio 增加：(1) aggregate std 单调下降（convergence 增强）， (2) pairwise Jaccard 轻微下降（per-example overlap 减少，divergence 增强）， (3) net effect asymmetry 增加（每种架构的 \\\"helped bias\\\" 越来越不同）。 这三个轨迹在 attention ratio 维度上高度相关（ρ≈-0.95），但 n=4 datapoints（h0 无 attention， 无 per-example divergence metric），p=0.05 只是 borderline。 核心 insight：更多 attention → aggregate 更 similar，但 per-example mechanism 更 different。 这是 underspecification 的具体量化——\\\"the HOW diverges while the WHAT converges\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n    \"description\": \"在 StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 上运行 1.3B 模型，寻找 second convergence anchor\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"benchmarks_evaluated\": [\n        \"StoryCloze\",\n        \"BoolQ\",\n        \"COPA\"\n      ],\n      \"StoryCloze\": {\n        \"rho\": -0.7,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.117,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.031,\n          0.025,\n          0.02,\n          0.018,\n          0.015\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 52,\n        \"direction\": \"consistent with LAMBADA\",\n        \"significant\": false,\n        \"suggestive\": true\n      },\n      \"BoolQ\": {\n        \"rho\": -0.8,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.028,\n          0.024,\n          0.018,\n          0.014,\n          0.01\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 64,\n        \"direction\": \"consistent with LAMBADA\",\n        \"significant\": false,\n        \"suggestive\": true\n      },\n      \"COPA\": {\n        \"rho\": -0.3,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.55,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.045,\n          0.042,\n          0.044,\n          0.04,\n          0.038\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 16,\n        \"direction\": \"weak, inconsistent\",\n        \"significant\": false,\n        \"suggestive\": false\n      },\n      \"best_new_benchmark\": \"BoolQ\",\n      \"best_new_rho\": -0.8,\n      \"best_new_p\": 0.083,\n      \"updated_bh_fdr\": {\n        \"LAMBADA_adj_p\": 0.075,\n        \"BoolQ_adj_p\": 0.375,\n        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.375,\n        \"note\": \"BH-FDR with 9 benchmarks: LAMBADA adj-p improves from 0.100 to 0.075 but still >0.05; BoolQ does not survive\"\n      },\n      \"n_benchmarks_bh_fdr_significant\": 1,\n      \"n_suggestive_p_below_0_15\": 3,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Extended benchmark convergence analysis (1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Task Type\",\n          \"ρ\",\n          \"Exact p (2-tail)\",\n          \"Std Reduction %\",\n          \"Suggestive (p<0.15)?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"last-word retrieval\",\n            -1.0,\n            0.017,\n            \"79%\",\n            \"Yes (significant)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BoolQ\",\n            \"passage yes/no\",\n            -0.8,\n            0.083,\n            \"64%\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StoryCloze\",\n            \"context completion\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.117,\n            \"52%\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy*\",\n            \"factual QA (GDN-excl)\",\n            -0.9,\n            0.083,\n            \"—\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"COPA\",\n            \"causal reasoning\",\n            -0.3,\n            0.55,\n            \"16%\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"commonsense reasoning\",\n            0.3,\n            0.742,\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"multi-step reasoning\",\n            0.6,\n            0.883,\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Winogrande\",\n            \"coreference reasoning\",\n            0.1,\n            0.95,\n            \"—\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU†\",\n            \"knowledge QA\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Excluded (GDN artifact)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Updated BH-FDR correction (9 benchmarks)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rank\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Raw p\",\n          \"BH threshold\",\n          \"BH adj-p\",\n          \"Significant?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            0.017,\n            0.006,\n            0.075,\n            \"No (improved from 0.100)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"BoolQ\",\n            0.083,\n            0.011,\n            0.375,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            0.117,\n            0.017,\n            0.375,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"StoryCloze\",\n            0.117,\n            0.022,\n            0.375,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            0.35,\n            0.028,\n            0.63,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            6,\n            \"COPA\",\n            0.55,\n            0.033,\n            0.825,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            7,\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.683,\n            0.039,\n            0.878,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"Winogrande\",\n            0.95,\n            0.044,\n            0.95,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            9,\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"excl\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Excluded\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Exp-011 在 median 档下不产生 second significant anchor（BH-FDR 仍仅 LAMBADA 在 uncorrected 下显著）， 但产生有价值的 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的 statistical argument 变为： \\\"While no single additional benchmark reaches significance after correction, the consistent negative direction across retrieval-heavy tasks (LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, BoolQ ρ=-0.8, StoryCloze ρ=-0.7, GDN-excluded ARC-Easy ρ=-0.9) versus null/positive results on reasoning tasks suggests the convergence effect is systematically related to task type rather than a LAMBADA-specific artifact.\\\" 这是 honest framing——不 overclaim significance，但通过 direction consistency + task taxonomy 构建 reasonable evidence。对 EMNLP Findings 足够，但 Main 困难。\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：最佳新 benchmark (BoolQ) ρ≈-0.8, p≈0.083（suggestive, not significant）。 BoolQ 作为 passage-based yes/no task，其核心操作是从给定 passage 中 retrieve 关键信息来判断命题真假， 与 LAMBADA 的 context retrieval 有结构相似性。因此 attention 的 equalizer 效应方向一致。 但 BoolQ 的 answer space 是 binary（yes/no），cross-architecture variance 的 baseline 本来就低， 加上 n=5 attention ratios 的 power limitation，p 值只能达到 suggestive 水平。 StoryCloze (ρ=-0.7, p=0.117) 也 suggestive——context completion task 的 retrieval 成分支持 convergence 方向，但效应弱于 LAMBADA。COPA (ρ=-0.3) 虽名为 causal reasoning from narratives， 实际 sample 太短（1-2 sentences），attention 的增量价值小且架构间差异不大。 BH-FDR 在 9 benchmarks 下将 LAMBADA adj-p 从 0.100 改善到 0.075——方向好但仍 >0.05， 所以 formal significance 仍然只有 LAMBADA（且仅在 uncorrected 下）。 但 3 个 benchmarks (LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze) 方向一致 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.9, p=0.083) 构成 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的论证从 \\\"single significant result\\\" 转为 \\\"consistent directional pattern across retrieval-heavy tasks\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":989,"startLine":1,"totalLines":989}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011EHbDy7C8NAcjStAZjzogw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n2\t\n3\t> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n7\t- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n8\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n9\t\n10\t## Paper Type\n11\tEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n12\t\n13\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n14\t\n15\t### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\n16\tAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n17\t\n18\t### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\n19\tThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\n22\tDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n23\t\n24\t## Story Spine\n25\t\n26\t### Problem\n27\tHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n28\t\n29\t### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\n30\tThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n31\t- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n32\t- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n33\t- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n34\t- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n35\t\n36\tOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n37\t\n38\t### Our Framing\n39\tWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n40\t\n41\t### Headline Result Template\n42\t\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n43\t\n44\t## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n45\t\n46\t### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\n47\tAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n48\t\n49\t### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\n50\tNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n51\t\n52\t### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\n53\tAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n54\t\n55\t### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\n56\tMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n60\t\n61\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n62\t\n63\t### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\n64\tResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\n65\tRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n66\t\n67\t### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n68\t**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n69\t1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n70\t2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n71\t3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n72\t4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n73\t5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n74\t6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n75\t\n76\tRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n77\t\n78\t### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\n79\tResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\n80\tRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n81\t\n82\t### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\n83\tResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n84\t\n85\t### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\n86\tResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n87\t\n88\t### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\n89\tResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03d14a9d-b512-4881-abb2-faf0a5ad3297","uuid":"4b99ffa8-e951-48f6-b3f8-c976fb20af5b","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:09:50.497Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n\n> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\nAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n\n### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\nThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n\n### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\nDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n\n### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\nThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n\nOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n\n### Our Framing\nWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n\n## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n\n### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\nAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n\n### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\nNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n\n### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\nAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n\n### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\nMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\nResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\nRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n\n### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n\nRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n\n### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\nResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\nRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n\n### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\nResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n\n### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\nResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n\n### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\nResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QsRPeHyDUDaaVDDVuk9uQJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill for guidance on writing style.\n\nLet me now write the full LaTeX paper. I need to cover:\n\n1. All 10 experiments (one is cancelled - 7B model)\n2. Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, Conclusion\n3. Claims: Task-Dependent Convergence, Scale-Dependent Convergence, Per-Example Divergence\n4. Honest framing, EMNLP Findings target\n\n\n5. 20+ references in Related Work\n6. Tables for each experiment\n\nI'm structuring the paper with an abstract and introduction laying out the problem and contributions, then a related work section covering ensemble diversity, underspecification, and dataset cartography. The methodology section will detail the experimental setup and metrics, followed by results organized around my three main claims—task-dependent convergence, scale-dependent convergence, and per-example divergence—each supported by specific experiments with accompanying tables.\n\nNow I'm planning the remaining results sections on attention characterization and statistical robustness, then a discussion that differentiates this work from Wang et al. and addresses limitations. I need to write the LaTeX carefully, pulling data directly from the experiment files without overclaiming, and keeping everything within the 8-page EMNLP Findings limit while ensuring all key experiments and tables are included.\n\nWriting the paper now... I'm realizing I need to clarify the experiment indexing—exp-008 actually splits into two parts: the surface features analysis with perplexity and cross-architecture tests, and then the statistical robustness framework with bootstrap and multiple comparison corrections. Let me map out which experiments correspond to which indices in my list.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the paper structure for EMNLP 2026 format. I need to fit everything into about 8 pages of main text while including all the experimental tables, proper citations, and maintaining honest framing throughout. I'll organize it into sections covering task-dependent convergence, scale-dependent effects, and the per-example divergence patterns that emerge despite aggregate convergence, then move into the statistical validation work. I'm realizing I have way too many tables for an 8-page paper—I need to consolidate strategically. The core tables should be the extended benchmark results, per-example overlap metrics, the 340M rebound analysis, a combined perplexity and statistical test table, the multiple comparison and sensitivity checks, and the convergence-divergence patterns, with attention statistics moved to the appendix.\n\nActually, I can fit all seven tables if I keep them compact. Let me just start writing the paper using the ACL 2023 template.\n\nWriting the LaTeX document... Augmented Linear Recurrent Models. Let me write out the full LaTeX now—this will be comprehensive.\n\nI'm compiling the complete reference list, working through the key papers on model architectures like Mamba, RetNet, and HGRN2, foundational transformer work, linear attention mechanisms, recent hybrid approaches, and the benchmark datasets and evaluation frameworks I'll need to cite.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17423,"cache_read_input_tokens":23569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17423},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03d14a9d-b512-4881-abb2-faf0a5ad3297","uuid":"4c4a9691-2548-4bd3-a7e6-625337b8d351"}
